### Why the Previous Versions Failed on Your Test Sites:
1. **DOM vs. Network Detection**: Sites like `godaddy.com`, `curlie.org`, and `patriotsquare.us` load scripts dynamically or route them via inline service-workers/asynchronous XHR/Fetch requests. Scanning solely DOM tags misses background network tracking. This rewrite integrates the **`webRequest` API** alongside DOM checks to catch real-time calls to `googlesyndication.com`, `com.cdn.cloudflare.net`, `firestore.googleapis.com`, `d1cq301dpr7fww.cloudfront.net`, and more.
2. **CSS Specificity Clashes**: Websites with modern CSS frameworks (like `mamma.com` and `activesearchresults.com`) reset or override button styles, text colors, and font rendering. This build isolates the entire blocking interface inside a **Closed Shadow DOM (`attachShadow({ mode: "closed" })`)**, completely shielding the overlay from host-page styles.
3. **Tab Renaming & Link Styler**: Merges the core functional design of **GAFALink**: outbound hyperlinks to GAFAM and proprietary domains are styled with custom highlights (red background/yellow text), and whenever a page is covered, the tab title is dynamically modified to prepend `[Googless Blocked]`.
4. **Whitelisting**: Adds support for persistent exclusion lists (e.g., `startpage.com`) directly managed via storage and the popup.

